From 00e591ed09f01084c6ab5a62537bf1221537573e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:35 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 11/14] ipa: libipa: Add contrast detection autofocus algorithm

Add an autofocus algorithm based on a contrast measurement over a grid
of regions, for IPA modules whose statistics provide no phase detection
data.

The algorithm implements the libcamera autofocus controls (AfMode,
AfRange, AfSpeed, AfMetering, AfWindows, AfTrigger, AfPause and
LensPosition) and reports AfState, AfPauseState, LensPosition and
FocusFoM. Its structure follows the contrast detection part of the
Raspberry Pi autofocus algorithm, and so does the tuning data format:
lens positions are in dioptres, mapped to lens driver units through a
piecewise linear function, and scans are parametrised per range and
speed. A coarse scan, reversed when the peak may lie behind its start,
is followed by a fine scan around the interpolated peak. In continuous
mode, a change in the contrast or brightness of the focus area followed
by a stable period starts a new scan.

The statistics are only used once a configurable number of frames has
elapsed after each lens movement, which lets IPA modules account for
the latency between a lens command and the statistics of the first
frame captured with the lens in its new position.

[backport: use libcamera::Span for the AfWindows control default, as the
 v0.7.2 control API predates the switch to std::span]

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
